{"text": "The Bells.\n\nPaloma held Jonas's arm. Her heart jumped.\n\nThe first shape came closer. It had four thin legs and a long face. It had a little beard. Around its neck, there was a bell.\n\nThen it opened its mouth and made a funny noise.\n\nPaloma started to laugh. \"It's a goat! Jonas, it's only a goat!\"\n\nThere were more behind it. Ten, fifteen, twenty. Brown ones, white ones, black ones. Every animal had a bell.\n\nThey walked past the rock, one after another. They were not interested in two cold children.\n\nOne small white goat stopped. It looked at Paloma's chocolate paper. Then it ate the paper.\n\n\"Hey!\" said Paloma. It ran back to the others.\n\n\"Look,\" said Jonas. \"They aren't eating grass. They're all walking the same way.\"\n\nIt was true. They walked quickly down the hill, in a long line. They looked like children after school.\n\n\"Where do goats go in the evening?\" asked Paloma.\n\n\"Home,\" said Jonas. Then his eyes opened wide. \"Paloma, goats live on farms. Farms have houses. And houses have people.\"\n\n\"But we don't know these goats,\" said Paloma. \"Maybe they're going to the other side of the mountain.\"\n\n\"Maybe,\" said Jonas. \"But it's half past five. It's going to be dark soon. We can't sit here.\"\n\nPaloma looked at the fog. Then she looked at the animals.\n\nThe last one was big and old. It walked slowly, and its bell had a deep sound.\n\nPaloma thought about Mrs Berg's voice. If you are lost, listen.\n\nShe listened. The bells were going down, down, down the mountain.\n\n\"OK,\" Paloma said. She stood up and held out her hand. \"We're going to follow them.\"", "textSha256": "e7e6eb8985f8d01a8e4110a42b18e80deda975e59961e870d17e4062ba1e0caa", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "speed": 0.95, "lang": "en", "parts": 1, "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "B", "e", "l", "l", "s", ".", "\n", "\n", "P", "a", "l", "o", "m", "a", " ", "h", "e", "l", "d", " ", "J", "o", "n", "a", "s", "'